<title>FINLAND: Finnish Nov exports through ports up 11.6 pct y/y. [CORRECTED 08:47 GMT]</title>
<headline>Finnish Nov exports through ports up 11.6 pct y/y. [CORRECTED 08:47 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline and first paragraph to read exports rose rather than fell, and corrects amount.)</p>
<p>Finnish exports through ports</p>
<p>rose 11.6 percent year-on-year in November to 3.11 million tonnes, the Board of Navigation said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>But in January-November, exports through ports fell 2.8</p>
<p>percent year-on-year to 30.57 million tonnes.</p>
<p>November imports through ports rose 1.6 percent to 3.33</p>
<p>million tonnes and January-November imports fell 0.2 percent to</p>
<p>33.48 million tonnes, the board said.</p>
<p>The Board of Navigation gave the following statistics of</p>
<p>foreign trade via ports (tonnes unless stated):</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>			   ----------------- 1996 --------------------</p>
<p>			  Nov     change yr/yr Jan-Nov  change yr/yr</p>
<p> TOTAL (mln tonnes) 3.110     +0.324	 30.57	  -0.887</p>
<p> of which</p>
<p> Paper		731,846    +69,419     7,344,651     -625,189</p>
<p> Pulp		 132,906    +52,992     1,359,051     +220,958</p>
<p> Sawn goods	 359,374    -2,972	3,190,482     -311,808</p>
<p> Chemicals	  200,190    +25,036     2,022,582     -766,565</p>
<p> Metals,</p>
<p> metal products   194,967    +10,832     1,959,543     -243,477</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p>			   ----------------- 1996 --------------------</p>
<p>			  Nov     change yr/yr Jan-Nov   change yr/yr</p>
<p> TOTAL (mln tonnes) 3.327	+0.507     33.476	 -0.717</p>
<p> of which</p>
<p> Crude oil	  576,673    -338,240    6,211,867   -1,331,722</p>
<p> Oil products     316,491    +109,405    3,599,456     +984,933</p>
<p> Raw minerals,</p>
<p> cement	     319,545    -91,108     3,192,001     -404,768</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
